<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; FONT-WEIGHT: bold; DISPLAY: inline"><a name="conflictsother">Conf</a>licts Regarding Other Activities of Affiliates of the General Partner</font></div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt" align="left">&#160;</div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="left"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">Management of the general partner intends to devote to the Partnership the time and attention considered necessary for the proper management of the Partnership&#8217;s activities. However, management of the general partner will engage in unrelated business activities, either for their own account or on behalf of other partnerships, joint ventures, corporations, or other entities in which they have an interest. This creates a continuing conflict of interest in allocating management time. See &#8220;Risk Factors &#8212; Risks Inherent in an Investment in Us.&#8221;&#160;&#160;Officers of the general partner and its affiliates may manage other businesses and will not devote their time exclusively to managing the Partnership and its business, and the Partnership may face additional competition for time and capital because neither the general partner nor its affiliates are prohibited from raising money for or managing other entities that pursue the same types of investments that the Partnership targets.</font></div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt" align="left">&#160;</div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="left"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">Affiliates of the general partner will not be restricted from participating in other businesses or activities, even if these other businesses or activities compete with the Partnership&#8217;s activities and operate in the same areas as the Partnership.</font></div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="left">&#160;</div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="left">
<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; FONT-WEIGHT: bold; DISPLAY: inline"><a name="conflictsrelatingdealings"><!--EFPlaceholder--><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; FONT-WEIGHT: bold; DISPLAY: inline">Conflicts </font></a>Relating to Dealings Between Affiliates of the General Partner and Affiliates of the Manager</font></div>

<div style="DISPLAY: block; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><br>
<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="left"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">Entities controlled by the owners of our general partner have made investments in, loaned money to and otherwise engaged in transactions with affiliates of the Manager in the past, and expect to do so in the future.&#160;&#160;The following is a description of those transactions that are on-going as of the date of this prospectus.</font></div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="left"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Times New Roman; DISPLAY: inline">&#160;</font></div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="left"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">As described below, Mr. Knight was responsible for the organization of Apple REIT Ten, Inc.&#160;&#160;Mr. Knight is the chairman and chief executive officer of Apple REIT Ten, Inc. and owns its advisory company.&#160;&#160;Mr. McKenney is the President of Capital Markets of Apple REIT Ten, Inc. and Mr. Keating serves on its board of directors.&#160;&#160;As a result, Apple REIT Ten, Inc. may be deemed an affiliate of both the Partnership and our general partner.&#160;&#160;On June 2, 2014, Apple Ten Ventures Services, Inc., a wholly owned subsidiary of Apple REIT Ten, Inc., acquired preferred member interests in American Energy Partners Holdco, LLC (&#8220;Holdco&#8221;), which is an Oklahoma limited liability company controlled by Mr. McClendon.&#160;&#160;In addition, on May 28, 2013, Cripple Creek Energy, LLC, a company under common control of the Manager, was formed (&#8220;Cripple Creek&#8221;).&#160;&#160;Cripple Creek raised $100 million from the sale of its preferred member interests to Apple Ten Ventures Services, Inc. to fund a portion of the acquisition and development costs of its oil and gas properties and related investments.&#160;&#160;&#160;The preferred member interests in Cripple Creek were redeemed in full in November 2014 for par plus accrued and unpaid dividends.</font></div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="left"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Times New Roman; DISPLAY: inline">&#160;</font></div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="left"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">In 2013 and 2014, entities owned by Mr. Keating and Mr. Mallick and members of their immediate families acquired indirect ownership interests in American Energy Ohio Holdings LLC (&#8220;AEU&#8221;) and American Energy Woodford Holdings, LLC, (&#8220;AEW&#8221;).&#160;&#160;Mr. Merritt also acquired interests in AEW through an entity he controls. The interests were acquired by the entities owned by Mr. Keating, Mr. Mallick and Mr. Merritt on the same terms as other similarly situated investors in each of those entities.&#160;&#160;AEU and AEW were formed by affiliates of the Manager for the purpose of acquiring properties in the Utica Shale and Woodford Shale.&#160;&#160;While we are not prohibited from acquiring oil and gas properties in those areas, the Manager is not required to recommend to us opportunities to acquire properties in those areas and we do not expect to acquire properties in those areas at this time or in the near future and thus, we do not expect to compete with AEU and AEW.</font></div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="left"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Times New Roman; DISPLAY: inline">&#160;</font></div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="left"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">Mr. Keating and Mr. Mallick, through entities owned by Mr. Keating and Mr. Mallick and members of their immediate families, and Mr. McKenney have committed to acquire indirect ownership interests in American Energy &#8211; Permian Basin, LLC (&#8220;AEPB&#8221;) and American Energy - Marcellus, LLC (&#8220;AEM&#8221;) on the same terms as other similarly situated investors in AEPB and AEM, respectively.&#160;&#160;AEPB and AEM were formed by affiliates of the Manager for the purpose of acquiring properties in the Southern Wolfcamp play area of the Central Permian Basin in West Texas and the liquids rich area of the Marcellus Shale in Ohio, Pennsylvania and West Virginia. While we are not prohibited from acquiring oil and gas properties in those areas, the Manager is not required to recommend to us opportunities to acquire properties in those areas and we do not expect to acquire properties in those areas at this time or in the near future and thus, we do not expect to compete with AEPB and AEM.</font></div>

<div style="DISPLAY: block; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><br>
</div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="left">
<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="left"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Times New Roman; DISPLAY: inline">On December 29, 2014, an entity controlled by Mr. Keating and Mr. Mallick, and owned by entities owned by Mr. Keating and Mr. Mallick and members of their immediate families, closed a sale transaction for a parcel of improved real property located in Nichols Hills, Oklahoma to an entity controlled by Mr. McClendon for $3.0 million.&#160;&#160;</font></div>
</div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="left">&#160;</div>

