<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">&#160;</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">Each member of our general partner has the right to appoint one person to the general partner&#8217;s board of directors.&#160;&#160;All decisions regarding the business of our general partner and our Partnership will be made by the board of directors of our general partner at meetings of the board of directors at which a quorum is present.&#160;&#160;The presence of a majority of the directors constitutes a quorum, and the vote of a majority of a quorum constitutes a decision by the board of directors.</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; DISPLAY: block; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><br>
</div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">The owners of the members of our general partner have granted each other the right of first refusal to acquire any interests in the members of our general partner that the owners propose to sell.&#160;&#160;If the owners of the members of our general partner do not exercise the right of first refusal, the purchaser of the owner of our general partner will have the right to appoint a member to our board of directors, and if a person or group of affiliated persons were to acquire a controlling interest in three of the owners of our general partner, the person would be able to control our general partner and the Partnership.&#160;&#160;Our Partnership Agreement does not give the holders of common units the right to cause an owner of our general partner to exercise its buy-sell right, or provide the holders the right to consent to or otherwise approve the transfer by an owner of our general partner of its membership interest in our general partner.&#160;&#160;Our general partner does, however, agree not to permit a change of control of our general partner to occur.&#160;&#160;A change of control is defined as a person who is not currently a beneficial owner of our general partner or a &#8220;qualifying owner&#8221; becoming the beneficial owner of 50% or more of the membership interest in our general partner.&#160;&#160;A qualifying owner generally is defined as the following with respect to the current beneficial owners of our general partner:&#160;&#160;conservators, guardians, executors, administrators, and similar persons of any trust, private foundation or custodianship that such beneficial owner, his spouse, lineal descendants or estate is a beneficiary.</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt">&#160;</div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; FONT-WEIGHT: bold; DISPLAY: inline"><a name="relationshipsbetweenowners"><!--EFPlaceholder--><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; FONT-WEIGHT: bold; DISPLAY: inline">Relationships </font></a>Between the Owners of the General Partner and the Manager and its Affiliates</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; DISPLAY: block; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><br>
</div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline"><font id="TAB1" style="MARGIN-LEFT: 36pt"></font>Entities controlled by the owners of our general partner have made investments in, loaned money to and otherwise engaged in transactions with affiliates of the Manager in the past, and expect to do so in the future.&#160;&#160;The following is a description of those transactions that are on-going as of the date of this prospectus.</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; DISPLAY: block; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><br>
</div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt">
<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt">
<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="left"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">As described below, Mr. Knight was responsible for the organization of Apple REIT Ten, Inc.&#160;&#160;Mr. Knight is the chairman and chief executive officer of Apple REIT Ten, Inc. and owns its advisory company.&#160;&#160;Mr. McKenney is the President of Capital Markets of Apple REIT Ten, Inc. and Mr. Keating serves on its board of directors.&#160;&#160;As a result, Apple REIT Ten, Inc. may be deemed an affiliate of both the Partnership and our general partner.&#160;&#160;On June 2, 2014, Apple Ten Ventures Services, Inc., a wholly owned subsidiary of Apple REIT Ten, Inc., acquired preferred member interests in American Energy Partners Holdco, LLC (&#8220;Holdco&#8221;), which is an Oklahoma limited liability company controlled by Mr. McClendon.&#160;&#160;In addition, on May 28, 2013, Cripple Creek Energy, LLC, a company under common control of the Manager, was formed (&#8220;Cripple Creek&#8221;).&#160;&#160;Cripple Creek raised $100 million from the sale of its preferred member interests to Apple Ten Ventures Services, Inc. to fund a portion of the acquisition and development costs of its oil and gas properties and related investments.&#160;&#160;&#160;The preferred member interests in Cripple Creek were redeemed in full in November 2014 for par plus accrued and unpaid dividends.</font></font></div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="left">&#160;</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="justify">
<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt" align="justify">
<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">In 2013 and 2014, entities owned by Mr. Keating and Mr. Mallick and members of their immediate families acquired indirect ownership interests in American Energy Ohio Holdings LLC (&#8220;AEU&#8221;) and American Energy Woodford Holdings, LLC, (&#8220;AEW&#8221;).&#160;&#160;Mr. Merritt also acquired interests in AEW through an entity he controls. The interests were acquired by the entities owned by Mr. Keating, Mr. Mallick and Mr. Merritt on the same terms as other similarly situated investors in each of those entities.&#160;&#160;AEU and AEW were formed by affiliates of the Manager for the purpose of acquiring properties in the Utica Shale and Woodford Shale.&#160;&#160;While we are not prohibited from acquiring oil and gas properties in those areas, the Manager is not required to recommend to us opportunities to acquire properties in those areas and we do not expect to acquire properties in those areas at this time or in the near future and thus, we do not expect to compete with AEU and AEW.</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt">&#160;</div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt">
<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">Mr. Keating and Mr. Mallick, through entities owned by Mr. Keating and Mr. Mallick and members of their immediate families, and Mr. McKenney have committed to acquire indirect ownership interests in American Energy &#8211; Permian Holdings LLC (&#8220;AEPB&#8221;) and American Energy - Marcellus Holdings LLC (&#8220;AEM&#8221;) on the same terms as other similarly situated investors in AEPB and AEM, respectively.&#160;&#160;AEPB and AEM were formed by affiliates of the Manager for the purpose of acquiring properties in the Southern Wolfcamp play area of the Central Permian Basin in West Texas and the liquids rich area of the Marcellus Shale in Ohio, Pennsylvania and West Virginia. While we are not prohibited from acquiring oil and gas properties in those areas, the Manager is not required to recommend to us opportunities to acquire properties in those areas and we do not expect to acquire properties in those areas at this time or in the near future and thus, we do not expect to compete with AEPB and AEM.</font></div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="justify">&#160;</div>

<div id="PGBRK" style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt">
<div id="FTR">
<div id="GLFTR" style="WIDTH: 100%" align="center"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: Times New Roman; DISPLAY: inline">&#160; </font></div>
