<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">The monthly management fee will be in addition to all fixed rate charges under any joint operating agreements in which the Manager or any of its affiliates acts as operator and in which we own a working interest.&#160;&#160;In addition, we will reimburse the Manager for all third party costs incurred by it in performing services for us.</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Times New Roman; DISPLAY: inline">&#160;</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">Our ability to invest the net proceeds of the offering of the common units will depend on many factors, some of which are beyond our control, including the availability of suitable oil and gas properties for sale, availability of drilling rigs and other equipment and personnel to drill wells on our properties, oil and gas prices and other factors.</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; DISPLAY: block; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Times New Roman; DISPLAY: inline"><br>
</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; FONT-STYLE: italic; DISPLAY: inline">Class B Units</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Times New Roman; DISPLAY: inline">&#160;</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt">
<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="left"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">We will issue the class B units to an affiliate of the Manager. The class B units will entitle the holder to receive a portion of&#160;&#160;distributions made after Payout.&#160;&#160;See &#8220;Capital Contributions and Distributions.&#8221;</font></div>
</div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; FONT-STYLE: italic; DISPLAY: inline">&#160;</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; FONT-STYLE: italic; DISPLAY: inline">Investment Opportunities</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Times New Roman; DISPLAY: inline">&#160;</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">The Management Agreement provides that the Manager will use reasonable commercial efforts to identify oil and gas properties for acquisition by us that the Manager believes fall within the acquisition parameters set forth in this prospectus or established from time to time by agreement between us and the Manager.&#160;&#160;Although the Manager is not required to refer to us any specific amount of oil and gas properties for acquisition, we may terminate the Management Agreement if the Manager does not refer to us one or more oil and gas property acquisitions reasonably capable of consummation for a 60 day period during which we have notified the Manager that we have available capital contributions and borrowing available under our credit facility, which have not been spent or reserved for expenditure by us.&#160;&#160;If we terminate the Management Agreement under these circumstances, a portion of the class B units issued to the Manager will be forfeit.&#160;&#160;See &#8220;Description of the Management Agreement &#8211; Termination.&#8221;</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Times New Roman; DISPLAY: inline">&#160;</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; DISPLAY: block; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt">
<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">Affiliates of the Manager have agreed to provide other entities the right to participate in opportunities affiliates of the Manager develop in the Southern Wolfcamp play area of the Central Permian Basin in West Texas, the Utica Shale and liquids rich portion of the Marcellus Shale areas in Ohio, Pennsylvania and West Virginia, and the Oklahoma Woodford Shale area of Central Northern Oklahoma, opportunities to <font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">acquire or </font>develop midstream assets in the continental United States and opportunities involving properties in the continental United States that consist exclusively of properties that will not be operated by the Manager or any of its affiliates, and the Management Agreement provides that the Manager is not required to offer us opportunities to acquire properties in those areas or that are exclusively properties that none of the Manager or any of its affiliates will operate.&#160;&#160;As a result, we do not expect to acquire any such oil and gas properties or assets identified by the Manager, however the Partnership is not prohibited from acquiring properties that it may identify for acquisition in any of these areas or that are exclusively properties that none of the Manager or any of its affiliates will operate.&#160;&#160;In addition, the Management Agreement provides that the Manager is not required to refer to us any properties that Aubrey K. McClendon or any entity of which he is an affiliate has an interest in or right to acquire pursuant to the Chesapeake Energy Corporation Founders Well Participation Program.</font></div>

