<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; FONT-STYLE: italic; DISPLAY: inline">Termination</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Times New Roman; DISPLAY: inline">&#160;</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">The Management Agreement is terminable by us if: (i) we sell all or substantially all of our assets; (ii) there is a change in control and the Manager is no longer controlled by Mr. McClendon or his immediate family; (iii) Mr. McClendon, the Manager&#8217;s key employee, ceases to be employed by the Manager and we do not approve of a proposed replacement of such key employee; (iv) the Manager becomes subject to bankruptcy proceedings; (v) the Manager materially breaches its obligations under the Management Agreement and does not cure the breach within 60 days of its receipt of notice of the breach; or (vi) the Manager or its affiliates defraud us or steal or misappropriate any of our assets and such circumstances have not been cured as provided in the Management Agreement.&#160;&#160;We may also terminate the Management Agreement if the Manager fails to recommend to us one or more acquisitions of producing or non-producing oil and gas properties that meet our acquisition parameters <font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">and</font> are reasonably capable of consummation at any time that we have an aggregate of at least $100 million <font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">consisting of</font> capital contributions received by us and which have not been spent by us,<font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">&#160;and</font> all available borrowings under our credit facility, in each case, that have not been reserved by us for any acquisitions, development operations or other expenses, which we refer to as Unallocated Funds, for a period of 60 consecutive days.</font></font></div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="justify"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Times New Roman; DISPLAY: inline">&#160;</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">The Management Agreement is terminable by the Manager if: (i) we become subject to bankruptcy proceedings; or (ii) we materially breach our obligations under the Management Agreement and do not cure the breach within 30 days of our receipt of notice of the breach.&#160;&#160;We and the Manager will have the right to cure certain of the events that cause termination.</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Times New Roman; DISPLAY: inline">&#160;</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">We and the Manager may also mutually agree to terminate the Management Agreement.</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Times New Roman; DISPLAY: inline">&#160;</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">We will initially issue to an affiliate of the Manager 100,000 class B units.&#160;&#160;If the Management Agreement is terminated by us because of a breach of the agreement by the Manager, or for fraud or theft by the Manager, then pursuant to the Partnership Agreement, the class B units will be forfeited and canceled.&#160;&#160;If we terminate the Management Agreement because of a change of control, because Mr. McClendon is no longer employed by the Manager or because of the bankruptcy of the Manager, then, pursuant to the Partnership Agreement,</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt">&#160;</div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt">
<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" id="hangingindent" width="100%" style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman">
<tr valign="top">
<td style="WIDTH: 72pt">&#160;</td>
<td style="WIDTH: 27pt">
<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: symbol, serif; DISPLAY: inline">&#183;</font></font></div>
</td>
<td>
<div align="left"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; DISPLAY: inline">If such termination occurs prior to the date we have invested all of our capital contributions, a number of the class B units will be forfeited and canceled equal to the number of class B units then outstanding multiplied by (a) 37.5% plus (b) 62.5% multiplied by a fraction, the numerator of which will be the amount of capital contributions that have not been invested prior to such date of termination and the denominator shall be the amount of the capital contributions we receive from common unitholders; and</font></font></div>
</td>
</tr></table>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt">
<div align="center">
<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" id="hangingindent" width="100%" style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman">
<tr valign="top">
<td style="WIDTH: 72pt">
<div><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">&#160; </font></div>
</td>
<td style="WIDTH: 27pt">
<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: symbol, serif; DISPLAY: inline">&#183;</font></font></div>
</td>
<td>
<div align="left">If the termination happens after we have invested all of our capital contributions but before a liquidity event then 37.5% of the class B units will be canceled and forfeited.</div>
</td>
</tr></table>
</div>
</div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt">
<div align="center">
<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" id="hangingindent" width="100%" style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman">
<tr valign="top">
<td style="WIDTH: 72pt">
<div><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">&#160; </font></div>
</td>
<td style="WIDTH: 27pt">
<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: symbol, serif; DISPLAY: inline">&#183;</font></font></div>
</td>
<td>
<div align="left"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; DISPLAY: inline">If the Management Agreement is terminated by us because of a failure to recommend acquisitions to us as described above, then a number of Class B units shall be forfeited equal to the number of class B units outstanding multiplied by a fraction (i) the numerator of which is the amount of Unallocated Funds at the date of termination, and the denominator of which is (ii) the aggregate amount of capital contributions received by us as of the date of such termination from the sale of common units<font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; DISPLAY: inline"> (less commissions, marketing fees and offering expenses) plus the amount of our borrowings and amounts of borrowings available to us under our credit facility</font><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; DISPLAY: inline">.&#160;&#160;If any of the class B units are canceled, the general partner will have the right to issue to another person who performs services for us a number of class B units equal to the number canceled.&#160;&#160;If any class B units are canceled, the amount that would have been distributed with respect to such canceled class B units will be distributed to the holders of common units until such time, if any, as the general partner causes us to issue class B units to another person who performs services for us.</font></font></font></div>
</td>
</tr></table>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="justify"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Times New Roman; DISPLAY: inline">&#160;</font></div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="justify"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">Except as set forth above, if the Management Agreement is terminated by us in connection with the sale of all or substantially all of our assets, or by the Manager because of our breach of the agreement, which is not cured as provided in the agreement or our bankruptcy, then the class B units remain issued and outstanding and unaffected by such termination.</font></div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt" align="justify">&#160;</div>

