<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt">&#160;</div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">(b)</font><font id="TAB2" style="COLOR: black; LETTER-SPACING: 9pt">&#160;</font><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">A prospective Limited Partner shall pay the subscription amount designated on his Subscription Agreement entirely in cash at the time of subscribing. A prospective Limited Partner shall not receive interest on the amount he pays from the time his subscription proceeds are deposited in the escrow account until his subscription proceeds are paid to the Partnership.</font> </font>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt" align="left"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">&#160;</font></div>
</div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; FONT-WEIGHT: bold; FONT-STYLE: italic; DISPLAY: inline">Section 5.8</font><font id="TAB2" style="COLOR: black; LETTER-SPACING: 9pt">&#160;</font><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; FONT-WEIGHT: bold; FONT-STYLE: italic; DISPLAY: inline">Incentive Rights.</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt">&#160;</div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt">
<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">On the date of this Agreement, the Partnership shall issue the Incentive Distribution Rights to the General Partner.</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt">&#160;</div>
</div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; FONT-WEIGHT: bold; FONT-STYLE: italic; DISPLAY: inline">Section 5.9</font><font id="TAB2" style="COLOR: black; LETTER-SPACING: 9pt">&#160;</font><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; FONT-WEIGHT: bold; FONT-STYLE: italic; DISPLAY: inline">Class B Units</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt">&#160;</div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">(a)</font><font id="TAB2" style="COLOR: black; LETTER-SPACING: 9pt">&#160;</font><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">At the Initial Closing and in consideration for services rendered or to be rendered to or for the benefit of the Partnership, the Partnership shall issue 100,000 Class B Units to the Class B Holder.&#160;&#160;Except as provided in <font style="TEXT-DECORATION: underline; DISPLAY: inline">Section 5.9(f)</font>, the Partnership shall not issue any additional Class B Units without the consent of the holders of a majority of the Outstanding Class B Units.</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: justify; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt">&#160;</div>

<div style="MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt" align="justify">&#160;</div>

<div>
<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">(b)&#160;&#160;</font><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">(i)&#160;&#160;If (A) the Management Agreement is terminated by the Operating Subsidiary pursuant to Section 10.2(b)(v) or Section 10.2(b)(vii) of the Management Agreement, then concurrently with such termination all of the Class B Units Outstanding shall be forfeited, cancelled and cease to be Outstanding.</font></div>
</div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt">&#160;</div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 72pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt">
<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">(ii)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;If (A) the Management Agreement is terminated by the Operating Subsidiary before the Full Investment Date, and (B) such termination by the Operating Subsidiary was made (I) at any time within 30 days after a Manager Change in Control, (II) in accordance with Section 8.2(b) of the Management Agreement because the Key Employees cease to be employed on a full time basis by the Manager or (III) during the Bankruptcy of the Manager, then concurrently with such termination a portion of the Class B Units Outstanding shall be forfeited, cancelled and cease to be Outstanding equal to the sum of (X) 37.5% of the Class B Units Outstanding plus (Y) a portion of the Class B Units Outstanding equal to the product of the Class B Units Outstanding immediately before such forfeiture multiplied by a fraction of which the numerator is (AA) the aggregate Capital Contributions made to the Partnership by the holders of Units that have not been invested, committed for investment or otherwise spent by the Partnership as of the date of such termination, and (BB) the denominator of which is the aggregate Capital Contributions made by holders of Units to the Partnership as of the date of such termination.</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Times New Roman; DISPLAY: inline"><br>
</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">(iii)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;If the Management Agreement is terminated by the Operating Subsidiary pursuant to Section 10.2(b)(vi) of the Management Agreement, then concurrently with such termination, a number of Class B Units shall be cancelled, forfeited and shall cease to be Outstanding equal to the number Class B Units Outstanding multiplied by a fraction the numerator of which shall be the amount of Unallocated Funds on the date of termination and the denominator of which shall be the total net Capital Contributions made to the Partnership (after deduction of Sales Commissions, Marketing Fees and Offering and Organization Expenses), plus the amount of borrowings outstanding under an Approved Credit Facility plus the amount that is available to be borrowed under an Approved Credit Facility, in each case as of the date of termination.</font></div>

<div style="DISPLAY: block; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Times New Roman; DISPLAY: inline"><br>
</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; DISPLAY: block; MARGIN-RIGHT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">(iv)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;If (A) the Management Agreement is terminated by the Operating Subsidiary&#160;&#160;on or after the Full Investment Date, and (B) such termination by the Operating Subsidiary was made (I) at any time within 30 days after a Manager Change in Control, (II) in accordance with Section 8.2(b) of the Management Agreement because the Key Employees cease to be employed on a full time basis by the Manager or (III)&#160;during the Bankruptcy of the Manager, then concurrently with such termination 37.5% of the Class B Units Outstanding shall be forfeited, cancelled and cease to be Outstanding.</font></div>

<br>
</div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">(c)</font><font id="TAB2" style="COLOR: black; LETTER-SPACING: 9pt">&#160;</font><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">Except as provided in this Section, the termination of the Management Agreement shall not forfeit, cancel or otherwise affect the Class B Units.&#160;&#160;If Class B Units are forfeited, cancelled and cease to be Outstanding pursuant to this Section 5.09, and there is more than one Record Holder of Class B Units, Class B Units will be forfeited, cancelled and cease to be Outstanding on a pro rata basis among the Record Holders, pro rata based on the number of Class B Units owned on the date of termination of the Management Agreement.</font></div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: justify; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt">&#160;</div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN-LEFT: 0pt; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">(d)</font><font id="TAB2" style="COLOR: black; LETTER-SPACING: 9pt">&#160;</font><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: times new roman; DISPLAY: inline">The forfeiture and cancellation of the Class B Units will not require the holder of such Class B Units or any former holder to repay any distribution previously made.</font></div>

